# Checkout on Windows converts LF to CRLF by default, which changes a file's
# bytes and so its hash. vendored.json records the hash of the vendored reader,
# so without this the vendor guard fails on Windows and nowhere else.
* text=auto eol=lf
# The NTFS fixture is a gzipped disk image. text=auto above would leave it alone
# because git detects it as binary, but saying so is cheaper than relying on the
# detection: a single converted byte would change the image and its hashes.
*.gz binary
*.img binary
